{"id":"word:hebrew:H1616","type":"word","title":"גֵּר","subtitle":"H1616 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, a guest ; by implication, a foreigner","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to גֵּר (H1616) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 92 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"גֵּר (gêr) means properly, a guest ; by implication, a foreigner First listed occurrence: 1Chr 22 2."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"גֵּר","transliteration":"gêr","pronunciation":"gare","strong":"H1616","lemmaId":"hebrew:H1616","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["גֵּ֣ר","וְ/לַ/גֵּ֖ר","גֵרִ֥ים","לַ/גֵּ֛ר","וְ/הַ/גֵּ֖ר"],"morphs":[["HNcmsa",22],["HTd/Ncmsa",13],["HC/Rd/Ncmsa",13],["HRd/Ncmsa",11],["HC/Td/Ncmsa",9],["HNcmpa",7],["HC/Ncmsc/Sp2ms",4],["HC/Ncmsa",4],["HTd/Ncmpa",2],["HR/Ncmsa",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, a guest ; by implication, a foreigner","usage":"alien, sojourner, stranger.","full":"H1616. ger גֵּר noun masculine Exod 12:48 sojourner (Arabic , Ethiopic Aramaic , גִּיּוֺר , prostelyte , גַּיֵּר proselytize , Phoenician גר in proper name, & plural גרם ) — גֵּר Gen 15:16 74t.; suffix גֵּרְךָ Exod 20:10 4 t., גֵּרוֺ Deut 1:16 ; plural גֵּרִים Exod 22:20 9 t., גֵּירִים 2Chr 2:16 ; — 1 sojourner , temporary dweller, new-comer (no inherited rights), compare Exod 12:19 ; Lev 24:16 ; Num 15:30 ; Josh 8:33 (opposed to homeborn ); of Abraham at Hebron Gen 23:4 (P; || תּוֺשָׁב ); Moses in desert Exod 2:22 (J) 18:3 (E; here explanation of name Gershom, Moses' son); as claiming hospitality Job 31:32 ; perhaps in above cases, and certainly in General, with technical sense; figurative of Yahweh Jer 14:8 ; of Israel in Egypt Gen 15:13 ; Exod 22:20 ; 23:9 (all J E) Lev 19:34 (H) Deut 10:19 ; 23:8 ; גֵּרִים with Yahweh Lev 25:23 (H) 1Chr 29:15 ; Psa 39:13 (in all || תּוֺשָׁב ) compare 119:19 . 2 usually of גֵּרים in Israel 2Sam 1:13 (Amalekite) compare Josh 8:33 , 35 (E) 20:9 (P) Isa 14:1 ; dwellers in Israel with certain conceded, not inherited right (compare RS OTJC 434; 2nd ed. 342. n.; K 42; Sem 75 f. Sta Geschichte.i.400 ). The גֵּר is to share in Sabbath rest Exod 20:10 ; 23:12 (both J E) Deut 5:14 ; otherwise he is have like obligations with Israel Exod 12:19 , 48 , 49 ; Lev 16:29 (all P) 17:8 , 10 , 12 , 13 , 15 ; 18:26 ; 20:2 ; 22:18 ; 24:16 , 22 (all H) Num 9:14 (twice in verse); 15:14-15 , (twice in verse); 15:16 , 26 , 29 , 30 ; 19:10 ; 35:15 (all P) Ezek 14:7 ; similar rights Deut 1:16 ; Ezek 47:22-23 , and like privileges Deut 16:11 , 14 ; 26:11 ; 29:10 ; 31:12 compare 2Chr 30:25 ; very rarely any distinction made, in obligation Lev 25:47 (3 t. in verse) (H), in permissible food Deut 14:21 ; in future success 28:43 ; kindness to גֵּר frequently enjoined: Lev 19:10 (|| עָנִי ), 23:22 (|| id. ) 19:34 (all H); Deut 10:18-19 , 14:29 ; 24:19-20 , 21 ; 26:12-13 , (all || וְאַלְמָנָה יָתוֺם ); oppression prohibited Lev 19:33 (H) Deut 24:14 ; Exod 22:20 ; 23:9 (twice in verse) (JE) Deut 24:17 ; 27:19 ; Jer 7:6 ; 22:3 ; Zech 7:10 (these eight || וְאַלְמָנָה יָתוֺם ); object of care to ׳י Psa 146:9 (|| id. ); charge that גֵּר has been oppressed Ezek 22:7 ; Mal 3:5 (both || id. ); also Ezek 22:29 (|| וְאֶבְיוֺן עָנִי ), Psa 94:6 ; compare also command that a poor brother be treated like גֵּר i.e. kindly, Lev 25:35 (H). Latest conception somewhat different: גֵּר 1Chr 22:2 ; 2Chr 2:16 ( הַגֵּירִים ) gathered for hard service; yet compare 30:25 . (Often with verbal cognate Exod 12:48-49 , Lev 16:29 ; 17:8 , 10 , 12 , 13 ; 18:26 ; 19:33 ; 20:2 ; Num 9:14 ; 15:14-15 , 16 , 26 , 29 ; 19:10 ; Josh 20:9 ; Ezek 47:22-23 , oft || תּוֺשָׁב Gen 23:4 ; Lev 25:23 , 35 , 47 ; 1Chr 29:15 ; Psa 39:13 ). [ גֵּיר ] noun masculine 2Chr 2:16 see גֵּר below I. גור .","rootNote":"or (fully) geyr (gare); from 1481 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 22 2","keyReferences":["1Chr 22 2","1Chr 29 15","2Chr 2 16","2Chr 30 25","2Sam 1 13","Deut 1 16","Deut 5 14","Deut 10 18"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":92,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 22 2","book":"1Chr","chapter":22,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/גֵּרִ֔ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 29 15","book":"1Chr","chapter":29,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גֵרִ֨ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmpa"},{"reference":"2Chr 2 16","book":"2Chr","chapter":2,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/גֵּירִים֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmpa"},{"reference":"2Chr 30 25","book":"2Chr","chapter":30,"verse":25,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/הַ/גֵּרִ֗ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Td/Ncmpa"},{"reference":"2Sam 1 13","book":"2Sam","chapter":1,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גֵּ֥ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"Deut 1 16","book":"Deut","chapter":1,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גֵּרֽ/וֹ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"Deut 5 14","book":"Deut","chapter":5,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/גֵֽרְ/ךָ֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncmsc/Sp2ms"},{"reference":"Deut 10 18","book":"Deut","chapter":10,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גֵּ֔ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"Deut 10 19","book":"Deut","chapter":10,"verse":19,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/גֵּ֑ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"Deut 10 19","book":"Deut","chapter":10,"verse":19,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גֵרִ֥ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmpa"},{"reference":"Deut 14 21","book":"Deut","chapter":14,"verse":21,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לַ/גֵּ֨ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HRd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"Deut 14 29","book":"Deut","chapter":14,"verse":29,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ֠/הַ/גֵּר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Td/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"Deut 16 11","book":"Deut","chap